  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry and tranquil weather is expected to continue\ninto early next week.\n\nRidging aloft and at the surface will continue to dominate the \nweather across region, providing several more days of quiet \nweather. The rex block should remain mostly intact into early \nnext week before slowly breaking down in favor of a more zonal \npattern by the middle of next week. Seasonable temperatures \nthrough Saturday will experience on a warming trend Sunday and \nMonday, with temperatures warming to as much as 10 degrees above\nnormal, with some normally warmer spots possibly approaching \n70F. A weak cold front moves through Monday, but the airmass is \nvery dry with ridging across the SW CONUS blocking any moisture \nreturn, the front will offer some cooler temperatures by \nTuesday.",
